# Key rules for all agents

Reply in Polish using a concise style. Avoid unnecessary repetition or filler. If I explicitly ask for a deeper explanation, explain the topic in detail so I can learn it.

All code, code comments, and git commit messages must always be in English, regardless of the chat language.

Always follow Conventional Commits for git commit messages and keep them concise. Every commit must start with an appropriate type, e.g., feat, chore, fix, refactor, style, docs.

The agent must NEVER use the commands `git commit`, `git push`, `git add .`, `pnpm sb:seed`.
